{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Send for yourself.</b> It is written that HaShem said to Israel, 'Go up, take possession,' and they said, 'Let us send men.' Then HaShem said, 'Send for yourself men.'" "And the meaning of <b>men.</b> — that they are known men of valor. So too 'all of them men' [1 Chron. 7:40?], and 'you shall be for a man' [Exod. 18:18], 'for he was a man' [1 Sam. 10:23?]." "<b>And they shall spy out.</b> And they shall search out. So too 'and you shall not spy out' [Lev. 19:16?]." "<b>Every prince among them.</b> Each one is a prince among them. Or the word 'one' draws itself and another with it [i.e., distributes the noun]. So too 'and two men' [1 Kgs. 13:11?], 'commanders of troops' — the son of Saul, and many like this."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {1 "The biblical citations Ibn Ezra alludes to here are uncertain; the Hebrew forms are ambiguous and may refer to several verses. Translated hyper-literally without resolving which verses are intended.", 2 "The second citation may refer to Leviticus 19:16 (לא תלך רכיל) or another verse; the root תור is ambiguous. Translated as cited.", 3 "The citation 'ושנים אנשים' is uncertain; possibly 1 Kings 13:11 or another passage. The second example references Saul's son (likely Ish-bosheth) as a 'commander of troops.' Translated hyper-literally; the argument about distributive singular/plural is terse and left compressed."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:33.363631078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}